# Review policy for the map's authored knowledge.
#
# THE CHANNEL IS THE FILENAME, which is why this needs no tooling at all:
# .coord/meta/<coord>/notes.jsonl, confirm.jsonl, docs.jsonl. The layout
# already put the channel in the path, so ordinary CODEOWNERS expresses
# the policy directly.
#
# The tiers are not arbitrary. `notes` is where somebody records a reason
# the code is the way it is - the part nobody can reconstruct - and it
# should be open to whoever learned it, including agents. `docs` and
# `confirm` are attestations ABOUT that content: a confirm says "I read
# this and it still holds", which is a claim only a maintainer can make
# on the project's behalf.
#
# Deliberately NOT owned: the derived index. .coord/index/, metrics/ and
# cache/ regenerate from source, so requiring review of them would put a
# human in front of a machine's output on every commit.

# Anyone may record what they learned.
.coord/meta/**/notes.jsonl

# Attestations and explanations are maintainer calls.
.coord/meta/**/confirm.jsonl   @whurleyjr734
.coord/meta/**/docs.jsonl      @whurleyjr734

# Lineage is identity: a bad edit here silently reattributes knowledge.
.coord/lineage/                @whurleyjr734

# The rules agents follow, and the lessons behind them.
CLAUDE.md                      @whurleyjr734
